31,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The staffing situation is worse than I feared. The late-turn pool is depleted, and we're relying on overtime for both final departures and overnight maintenance. We cannot promise more service without more people.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The pilots from eight years ago were actually successful, but the accessibility programme was a mixed bag. Some rebuilds worked, but the lane-priority stretches were just given back to traffic. We can't just trust the plan.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The pre-war shells are a risk; bidders are pricing in heavy contingencies because of unrecorded voids. Also, the ferry and rail offices haven't even agreed on passenger data terms. Coordination is a major hurdle.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The capital ledger has a ring-fenced construction balance from a lapsed grant, but the operating and technology lines were trimmed. Also, ticketing fees are now higher than our resurfacing budget. It's... worrying.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"The mid-city runs are taking way longer than they used to, but the crowds are clearing at the same rate! And the audits show people spend more time waiting for connections than at the ticket machines!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, if the delays are in the connections and not the ticketing, that changes things. But we still have the staffing crisis I mentioned; we can't simply add hours.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, that's why we need to look at what actually worked. The late-evening pilot was a success once, but if we don't have the staff now, it's just a dream.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, if the technology budget is trimmed but we have a ring-fenced construction balance, we should prioritize physical infrastructure over complex digital systems that require ongoing funding.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I suppose that makes sense, Toshio. But if the ticketing fees are already so high, I'm worried that any new system would just add more costs we can't afford in the long run.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Sakura,,But the journey audits show the machines aren't the problem! Maybe we can fix the travel time without spending a fortune on new technology?,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"If we can't add hours due to the roster crisis, we should avoid any plan that extends operating times. We need something that improves efficiency without adding more shifts.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, I agree. If the lane-priority stretches failed before, we should be cautious about bus corridors too. Maybe focusing on the stations is the safest bet?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the stations are risky. The contingency pricing for pre-war shells suggests that any work inside those structures could lead to unpredictable delays and cost overruns.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I don't want us to pick something that creates a huge debt for the future. If the technology budget is already trimmed, maybe a simple physical fix is better, provided it's not too expensive.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"But if the stations are too risky and the bus lanes failed before, what's left? We have to fix those mid-city delays! Maybe there's a way to do it without the old mistakes?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"We must be realistic. If the late-turn pool is this thin, any plan requiring more crew or overnight work is a non-starter. We need a solution that fits our current capacity.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm starting to think the only way forward is to find a plan that doesn't rely on the things we know are broken, whether that's the staffing or the old infrastructure.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, if we avoid the pre-war shells and the staffing crisis, we must also consider the lack of coordination between operators. A plan requiring multi-agency agreement is likely to stall.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just want to make sure we don't pick something that looks cheap now but costs us everything later. If the ticketing fees are already so high, we should be very careful.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I just want to help the passengers! If we can't do the stations or the night service, we have to find a way to make the mid-city trips faster!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"The candidates are now clear. Given the staffing crisis, the Night Service Extension is impossible. I believe the Crosstown Bus Corridor is the most viable option that fits our current capacity.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"I disagree, Victoria. The records show lane-priority stretches were returned to traffic before. I'm leaning toward the Integrated Fare Platform; it avoids the physical risks and staffing issues.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the Integrated Fare Platform requires coordination between ferry and rail offices that currently doesn't exist. I vote for the Crosstown Bus Corridor; it's the most straightforward.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about the fare platform because of those high contractor fees. But the bus corridor uses construction funds, which we actually have. I'll vote for the Crosstown Bus Corridor.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Sakura,,I want to fix those mid-city delays! The bus corridor is the only one that actually addresses the travel times I found in the audits. I vote for the Crosstown Bus Corridor!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,I'm satisfied with the consensus. The Bus Corridor addresses the mid-city delays Sakura found without exacerbating the staffing crisis I'm concerned about. I'll maintain my vote for the Crosstown Bus Corridor.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"I still have doubts about the lane-priority history, but if everyone else is convinced and the other options are truly impossible, I'll change my vote to the Crosstown Bus Corridor.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,It seems we have reached a rational agreement. I will maintain my vote for the Crosstown Bus Corridor.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel better knowing we're using the construction balance. I'll keep my vote for the Crosstown Bus Corridor.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Sakura,,Yay! I'm so glad we're doing this! I'll keep my vote for the Crosstown Bus Corridor too!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
